# --- Database ---
# SQL Server — the organization's own instance (docs/README.md "Database").
# No external/paid database service required, and NOT this app's job to
# create: the DBA pre-creates the database plus a dedicated schema named
# exactly "hearingmgr" (fixed — baked into prisma/migrations/'s committed
# SQL) and a login scoped to CONTROL on that schema only — never db_owner,
# never permission on any other schema in the database. See
# docs/README.md's "Deploying to Azure App Service" step 2 for the exact
# DBA-run T-SQL. `schema=hearingmgr` below is therefore required, not
# optional — a different value won't match the migration history at all.
#
# `encrypt=true` matches SQL Server 2022+'s default of requiring TLS; drop
# it (or set `encrypt=false`) against an older instance without a valid
# cert, or add `trustServerCertificate=true` instead of disabling
# encryption outright.
#
# For local dev without access to the org's instance, run SQL Server
# itself in a container (e.g. `docker run -e ACCEPT_EULA=Y
# -e MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD=<pw> -p 1433:1433
# mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest`), create the database +
# schema + scoped login exactly as docs/README.md describes (sa can do
# this once, locally — a real deployment never uses sa in DATABASE_URL),
# and point this at localhost — sqlite is NOT an option here (no
# enum/Json support), see docs/README.md "Local development".
DATABASE_URL="sqlserver://localhost:1433;database=hearing_manager;schema=hearingmgr;user=hearingmgr_app;password=YourStrong!Passw0rd;encrypt=true;trustServerCertificate=true"

# --- Server ---
# Azure App Service (Linux, Node) injects its own PORT — the app already
# reads it via `process.env.PORT ?? 3978`, so this only matters locally.
PORT=3978
# Only matters for CORS when the tab is hosted on a genuinely different
# origin than this backend. When co-hosted (backend/src/index.ts serves
# tab/'s build as static files — see "Deploying to Azure App Service" in
# docs/README.md), the browser never makes a cross-origin request in the
# first place, so this is effectively unused in that topology.
TAB_ORIGIN="https://localhost:53000"

# --- Microsoft Graph / Bot Framework ---
# These come from the Entra ID app registration described in
# docs/README.md section "Azure / Entra ID prerequisites". Until that
# registration exists, leave GRAPH_MODE=mock so the backend simulates
# Graph responses instead of calling out.
GRAPH_MODE=mock
MICROSOFT_APP_ID=
MICROSOFT_APP_PASSWORD=
MICROSOFT_APP_TENANT_ID=

# Fallback organizer/OnlineMeeting Graph identifiers, used by the Graph
# role-PATCH (graph/roleManager.ts) ONLY when a given Meeting row hasn't
# had its own organizerUserId/onlineMeetingId registered (see
# POST /api/meetings/:meetingId/register, routes/meetings.ts). This
# backend can serve many concurrent meetings at once (docs/README.md,
# "Multi-meeting") — these two vars only make sense as a convenience
# default for local dev / a single-meeting deployment, not as "the"
# meeting this backend manages.
ORGANIZER_USER_ID=
ONLINE_MEETING_ID=

# --- Auth (Teams SSO) ---
# AUTH_MODE=teams-sso (default) validates every /api/* request's
# Authorization: Bearer <token> header as a real Azure AD token minted for
# this app via Teams SSO — see backend/src/auth/verifyTeamsToken.ts and
# tab/src/teamsContext.ts. Requires MICROSOFT_APP_ID and
# MICROSOFT_APP_TENANT_ID above, plus TAB_HOSTNAME below (used to check the
# token's audience against api://<TAB_HOSTNAME>/<MICROSOFT_APP_ID>, matching
# manifest.json's webApplicationInfo.resource).
#
# AUTH_MODE=dev-bypass skips real token validation and trusts an
# x-actor-email header instead (or ?actorEmail= in the tab, see
# tab/src/teamsContext.ts dev fallback) — only for local dev without a real
# Entra app registration. NEVER set this in production: it lets any caller
# attribute audit-log entries to any judge they like.
AUTH_MODE=dev-bypass
TAB_HOSTNAME=

# Roster join/leave simulation (POST /api/meetings/:meetingId/roster/event)
# and the connection-health toggle are for local dev/testing only — the
# real bot never calls them over HTTP (see backend/src/bot/index.ts). Leave
# unset (disabled) outside of local dev.
ALLOW_ROSTER_SIMULATION=true

# --- Provisioning (server-to-server) ---
# POST /api/meetings/:meetingId/provision (routes/provision.ts) is how
# judges/auxiliaries and scheduled hearings + expected parties actually get
# into a meeting — the integration point for the court's case-management
# system, per docs/README.md §1 ("initial roles... assigned by another
# system"). Comma-separated list of accepted X-Api-Key values; rotate by
# adding the new key, updating the caller, then removing the old one. Unset
# (the default) disables the endpoint entirely (503). See docs/README.md
# "Provisioning" for the request shape and a curl example.
PROVISIONING_API_KEYS=

# --- Daily case-management import (pull, opposite direction from
# provisioning above) ---
# The backend calls the case-management system's own API once a day
# (services/dailyImportScheduler.ts + cmsClient.ts) to fetch TOMORROW's
# hearings and upsert them — see docs/README.md "Daily case-management
# import". CMS_MODE=mock (the default) returns a small built-in sample
# instead of calling out, so the whole pipeline is exercisable without a
# real CMS integration. Assumes Bearer-token auth against CMS_BASE_URL —
# adjust cmsClient.ts if the real system uses something else.
CMS_MODE=mock
CMS_BASE_URL=
CMS_API_KEY=
# Server-local hour (0-23) the daily pull runs at. Set the process's TZ
# env var if you need a specific timezone rather than server-default.
DAILY_IMPORT_HOUR=1
